# Build output
build/
*.log

# Closed-source upscaling runtimes (loaded at runtime from official NVIDIA/AMD SDKs)
Shaders/Upscaling/Streamline/*.dll
Shaders/Upscaling/FidelityFX/*.dll

# IDE / editor
.vs/
.vscode/
CMakeUserPresets.json

# vcpkg local installs
vcpkg_installed/

# Compiled artifacts
*.pdb
*.obj
*.ilk

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- 2026-09-18: MFG 调试期的备份/中间产物（不进版本库，避免 321 个未跟踪文件）---
src/*.bak-*
src/*.pre-*
src/*.keep-*
src/*.broken-*
src/backup-*/
# 2026-09-18: dated .bak-* snapshots of files that are themselves tracked
# (read_xray_log.py x10 in tools/, DynamicShaderFrameGen.ini x2 in
# SKSE/Plugins/). Together ~2MB of duplicates. They are pre-edit snapshots,
# i.e. git already stores the same information. The live files stay tracked.
*.bak
*.bak-*
tools/_tmp*
# 2026-09-18: 111 one-off diagnostic scripts accumulated during the MFG hunt.
# They were written to answer a single question each and are not maintained.
# The regression tools that ARE meant to be kept do not start with an
# underscore (tools/regress_v100_family.py, tools/regress_v102_camprev.py,
# tools/analyze_session.py, tools/snapshot.sh, tools/patch_*.py).
tools/_*
*.log
DLSSG-Transfusion.log
perf.csv

# 2026-09-18: regenerable outputs and pulled-out binaries.
#   reports/verdict_*.txt  - point-in-time verdicts from tools/read_xray_log.py.
#                            Once the build moves on they read as fact while
#                            describing a build that no longer exists, so they
#                            are regenerated rather than stored. read_log.bat
#                            (the wrapper that produces them) IS tracked.
#   _removed_*/            - third-party dlls pulled out of the game dir during
#                            triage; binaries, and copies of files that live
#                            outside this repo anyway.
reports/
_removed_*/

# --- 2026-09-24: pre-publication cleanup -------------------------------------
# MFG_MASTER_NOTES.md is a working ledger: local machine paths, full crash-log
# transcripts, and session-by-session notes. It is a development journal, not
# part of the plugin, and it has no place in the public source tree. Kept on
# disk, not in the repo.
MFG_MASTER_NOTES.md
MFG_MASTER_NOTES.md.bak-*
CHANGELOG.md.bak-*

# docs/runlogs/ - debug screenshots (PNG) and per-chapter drafts. 170 files at
# the time of writing, mostly one-off probes of a single run. Process artifacts.
docs/runlogs/

